  "id": "reflected-appraisals",
  "term": "reflected appraisals",
  "definition": "Reflected appraisals are a person’s views about themselves formed by taking another person’s perspective, such as considering how someone else sees their traits. In this sense, they differ from direct self-appraisals because they are indirect, third-person evaluations of the self.",
